ming patients families so you're  literally kind of going  yeah from patient to patient the ones  who are conscious at least  oh even if they're not conscious but  this was a special moment  the first time nikolai usachi responded  to his loved ones  since early december how long has he  been in intensive care  he's been more than 40 days from the 6th  of december  till now yeah that's that must be  very traumatic time for your family yes  but we never lost hope  we just prayed we thank god and we  prayed again  he's a miracle we just thank to god  on the eighth floor a step down from  intensive care  siddharla yusifi is slowly becoming less  dependent  on the equipment that's helping him to  breathe this is a massive improvement  over the last four days  exactly i appreciate is the end of the  world  apocalypse honestly is the apocalypse  can't breathe yeah  you feel very cold in the brain  in the brain very cold and freezing  and a lot of panic  a lot of panic i was i was feeling the  same is the end  this is really serious you have to take  it serious  i am one of the person who ignored  all the message unless sometimes i was  saying  this is not true this is but no  is it true can kill you  in the basement of the hospital patients  are looked after with the same care as  they were upstairs  we we care for patients they're patients  they're not you know they're still  patients  we treat them as they are but these are  the ones who didn't make it  there is no pacemaker  yeah there is nothing on the face or  ears  it's a bit you know heartbreaking coming  every day to do this  and still have people telling to your  face that this is not real or that this  is the flu  when you open these fridge doors  sometimes you must see some quite  young faces yes yes yes definitely  it's all ages really like uh  we have patients that they're my age or  even younger than me  um and there's older people who died for  coverage  uh yes enough that must shock you when  you when you 